      "id": "webhook-trigger",
      "name": "Webhook Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [240, 300],
      "webhookId": "inbound-replies"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Inbound Reply Handler\n\n**Purpose:** Process customer replies to payment reminders\n\n**Sources:**\n- SendGrid Inbound Parse (email replies)\n- Twilio SMS webhook (SMS replies)\n\n**Intents detected:**\n- STOP / UNSUBSCRIBE → suppress\n- PAID / \"I paid\" → verify payment\n- DISPUTE → escalate\n- PROMISE_TO_PAY → set promise date\n- HELP / ? → customer inquiry\n\n**Setup SendGrid Inbound Parse:**\n1. SendGrid → Settings → Inbound Parse\n2. Add: inbound.yourdomain.com → https://your-n8n.com/webhook/inbound-replies\n3. Configure MX records\n\n**Setup Twilio:**\n1. Twilio → Phone Numbers → Your Number\n2. Messaging → Webhook → https://your-n8n.com/webhook/inbound-replies\n3. HTTP POST",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "sticky-readme",
      "name": "README",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-200, 180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse inbound message (email or SMS)\nconst body = $input.item.json.body;\nconst headers = $input.item.json.headers;\n\nlet source, sender, messageBody;\n\n// Detect source (SendGrid Inbound Parse vs Twilio)\nif (body.from && body.text) {\n  // SendGrid Inbound Parse format\n  source = 'email';\n  sender = body.from;\n  messageBody = body.text || body.html || '';\n} else if (body.From && body.Body) {\n  // Twilio SMS format\n  source = 'sms';\n  sender = body.From;\n  messageBody = body.Body;\n} else {\n  source = 'unknown';\n  sender = null;\n  messageBody = '';\n}\n\nreturn {\n  source: source,\n  sender: sender,\n  message_body: messageBody.toLowerCase(),\n  raw_body: body\n};"
      },
      "id": "code-parse",
      "name": "Parse Inbound Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [460, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Classify intent from message body\nconst message = $input.item.json.message_body;\n\nlet intent = 'unknown';\nlet confidence = 0;\n\n// STOP / UNSUBSCRIBE\nif (message.match(/\\b(stop|unsubscribe|opt out|remove me)\\b/i)) {\n  intent = 'STOP';\n  confidence = 0.95;\n}\n// PAID\nelse if (message.match(/\\b(paid|payment sent|already paid|sent payment)\\b/i)) {\n  intent = 'PAID';\n  confidence = 0.85;\n}\n// DISPUTE\nelse if (message.match(/\\b(dispute|disagree|incorrect|wrong amount|never received)\\b/i)) {\n  intent = 'DISPUTE';\n  confidence = 0.80;\n}\n// PROMISE TO PAY (with date detection)\nelse if (message.match(/\\b(will pay|pay by|pay on|pay next week)\\b/i)) {\n  intent = 'PROMISE_TO_PAY';\n  confidence = 0.75;\n  \n  // Try to extract date\n  const dateMatch = message.match(/\\b(\\d{1,2}[\\/\\-]\\d{1,2}[\\/\\-]\\d{2,4})\\b/);\n  if (dateMatch) {\n    item.promise_date = dateMatch[1];\n  }\n}\n// HELP\nelse if (message.match(/\\b(help|question|\\?)\\b/i)) {\n  intent = 'HELP';\n  confidence = 0.70;\n}\n\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nitem.intent = intent;\nitem.confidence = confidence;\n\nreturn item;"
      },
      "id": "code-classify",
      "name": "Classify Intent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [680, 300]
